title: Bread for the Volga
subtitle: Russia is starving, and Münzenberg wants the party's help.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 3
max-visits: 1

= Bread for the Volga

The famine on the Volga has killed hundreds of thousands since the summer. Willi Münzenberg's Workers' International Relief collects money, flour and tools in every German city: posters of starving children hang in union halls that would never hang a communist poster.

Münzenberg wants the party's apparatus behind the campaign. The district treasurers point out that the party cannot pay its own printers.

- @all_in: Put the whole party behind the relief.
- @share: Help, but keep the party's money for the party.
- @joint: Make it a joint campaign with the unions and the SPD.

@all_in
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Wins sympathy far beyond the party, and Moscow is grateful.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds to give.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_famine = 1;
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.independence -= 2;
Q.world_revolution += 2;
Q.unity += 2;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

Ship after ship leaves Hamburg with flour and machine parts. Workers who have never read a communist paper put coins in our tins.

@share
subtitle: The party keeps its money; the campaign is smaller.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_famine = 2;
Q.worker_support += 1;
Q.independence += 1;
!}

The cells collect where they can. Münzenberg complains to Moscow that the Germans are mean.

@joint
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Bigger and less ours. The social democrats can share the credit.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any campaign with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e22_famine = 3;
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.spd_relation += 5;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 3;
!}

Some SPD branches join, and the ADGB lets its locals decide. The posters carry three names instead of one.
